      "score": 19,
      "text": "I built a quiz game around TypeSafe&#x27;s new Jev model, which has vision capabilities. Jev looks at a picture and a question and picks an answer (or taps a place) in about a quarter of a second.<p>I&#x27;ve always loved quiz games and thought this would be a fun way to see what it can do and how fast it is. I made the cards from scratch, and Jev gets exactly the picture you see. More cards will come over time.<p>Play against Jev on your own (there&#x27;s a leaderboard for each mode), or start a live match and challenge your friends, with Jev as one more player.<p>The code is open source, so feel free to build your own game or make more cards that I can publish.<p>Play: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;jevcards.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;jevcards.com</a>\nCode: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;Jose-Sabater&#x2F;jevcards\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;Jose-Sabater&#x2F;jevcards</a> (the newest cards stay private for a while)<p>Disclaimer: I ran Jev through both TypeSafe and Opper, and made the cards through Opper&#x27;s vision models and Claude Code. I work at Opper, but jevcards is open source and free to play.",
      "time": 1792509116,
      "title": "Show HN: Jev Cards, Can you beat a vision model at a picture quiz?",
